        "original_id": "e73a44af-4eca-5dbe-9f72-e8791f2a9735",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Ziegfeld Follies, The Life of Riley\n- People: Lucille Bremer, Irving Brecher, Fred Astaire, Lucille Ball, Fanny Brice, Judy Garland, Kathryn Grayson, Lena Horne, Gene Kelly, James Melton, Victor Moore, William Powell, Red Skelton, Esther Williams, William Bendix, Rosemary DeCamp, James Gleason\n- Companies: Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer\n- Roles: directors, screenwriters, actors, dancers\n\nFacts:\n- Shadow of the Thin Man was a screenplay written by Irving Brecher in 1941.\n- Ziegfeld Follies is a 1946 American musical comedy film released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.\n- Ziegfeld Follies was directed by Lemuel Ayers, Roy Del Ruth, Robert Lewis, Vincente Minnelli, Merrill Pye, George Sidney, and Charles Walters.\n- Ziegfeld Follies stars Fred Astaire, Lucille Ball, Lucille Bremer, Fanny Brice, Judy Garland, Kathryn Grayson, Lena Horne, Gene Kelly, James Melton, Victor Moore, William Powell, Red Skelton, and Esther Williams.\n- Fanny Brice was the only member of the Ziegfeld Follies ensemble who had been a star of the original Follies.\n- Lucille Bremer was an American film actress and dancer born on February 21, 1917, and she died on April 16, 1996.\n- The Life of Riley is a 1949 American comedy film directed by Irving Brecher and starring William Bendix, Rosemary DeCamp, and James Gleason.\n- Bye Bye Birdie was a screenplay written by Irving Brecher in 1963.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
